Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party material is included in this work.

Nothing is linked into the engine either: god-core has no runtime
dependencies. The Rust test suite links DuckDB (https://duckdb.org), MIT
licensed, to run generated queries and read the rows back — a development
dependency that is never distributed. The R and Python packages declare
dependencies (DuckDB; pandas in Python) that an install brings from their own
distributions, and their licenses travel with them. The printing backends
write source code for dplyr, pandas, polars and PySpark, which makes those
projects targets rather than dependencies: nothing of theirs is included.

Example datasets used in the book are named where they are used, with their
source and license, in the chapter that first shows them.
